    "title": "When Will Fortnite Servers Be Back Up? Fortnite March 19 Downtime, Explained",
    "text": "Fortnite players around the world have had their play sessions disrupted by server downtime, with the Epic Games title set to be unavailable for several hours on March 19. Server downtime is a regular occurrence for live-service titles like Fortnite, though that doesn’t make it any less frustrating if it disrupts your plans. If you’re wondering what’s going on with the Fortnite servers on March 19 and want to know when Fortnite will be playable again, Insider Gaming has all the details. When Will Fortnite Servers Be Back Up? Showdown. Image via Epic Games Fortnite servers are down for several hours for the start of Chapter 7, Season 2, though Epic Games has seemingly confirmed exactly when servers are expected to be back up. Downtime for the launch of Chapter 7, Season 2 begins at 2 AM ET, and an in-game countdown indicates downtime is expected to last for around five hours. More Insider Gaming: Is There a Live Event For Fortnite Chapter 7 Season 2? The countdown is due to end at 7 AM ET, indicating that this is when players should expect the doors to open for the new season. However, the times may still be subject to change, particularly if there any issues that arise while the patch is being deployed. The best place to keep an eye on the server status is social media. What’s In The Fortnite March 19 Update? The March 19 Fortnite update is the biggest in a long while, finally marking the start of Chapter 7, Season 2. Initially due to release on March 5, Epic Games delayed the start of the new season by two weeks, making Chapter 7, Season 1, the third-longest on record. The return of The Seven continues, with a head-to-head showdown against the Ice King, and artwork for the new season reveals Bugs Bunny is among those set to star. Other Looney Tunes characters are expected in the shop. More Insider Gaming: How to Register For Fortnite Save The World A teaser for the new season also showed several characters frozen by the Ice King, including Captain America, opening the door for another potential Marvel collab. As usual, the new season will see a sweep of changes to the Battle Royale landscape with new POIs, weapons, bosses, and more. What are you hoping to see in Fortnite Chapter 7, Season 2? Share your thoughts in the Insider Gaming Discord. For more Fortnite, read about the return to Google Play Store, and check out the teaser of a Super Meat Boy 3D crossover. MOBILE APP Level Up Your Gaming News Real-time news, exclusive podcasts, push alerts, and a better reading experience. Available on iOS & Android",
